.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite
*.db
checkpoints/
# Leading slash: the phase write-ups at the repo root, and nothing else. Without it
# this pattern matches any directory named analysis at any depth, which silently
# excluded src/analysis/ — the cost module would never have been committed and a
# fresh clone could not have run the report.
/analysis/
# Superseded hand-score directories, archived when a re-run or a change to the
# blinding invalidates them. Every version is already reachable in history, so a
# second copy under a new name only confuses which one is canonical. Ignored rather
# than left untracked because code_version() reads the whole tree: an untracked file
# makes every subsequent run record itself as produced from a dirty tree.
results/handscore_superseded/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/settings.json
docs/*.png